        "problem": "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7x-4y+6z=-1 \\\\ -2x+3y=0 \\\\ x-9y+z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $-4$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-2$ | $3$ | $0$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $0$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | {{field-4}} | $1$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7x-4y+6z=-1 \\\\ -2x+3y+0z=0 \\\\ x-9y+z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
